nce last purchase) and declining Frequency. They are at risk of churn.</p><p><strong>Recommended Strategy:</strong> Launch reactivation campaigns, discount incentives, reminder notifications, and feedback surveys to understand disengagement reasons and restore purchasing behavior.</p><p><strong>Business Objective:</strong> Reduce churn rate and re-engage inactive customers.</p><h2>5.6 Strategy for Low-Value or Infrequent Customers</h2><p>This group consists of customers with low Frequency and low Monetary values. While their current contribution is limited, they represent growth opportunities.</p><p><strong>Recommended Strategy:</strong> Provide entry-level promotions, educational content about product value, cross-selling opportunities, and automated nurturing campaigns to stimulate purchasing interest.</p><p><strong>Business Objective:</strong> Increase engagement and gradually move customers into higher-value segments.</p><h2>5.7 Strategic Implications</h2><p>The integration of RFM analysis with K-Means clustering enables data-driven decision-making in marketing strategy formulation. By aligning promotional efforts with customer behavioral profiles, businesses can optimize resource allocation, enhance customer satisfaction, and improve overall profitability. These targeted strategies ensure that each segment receives appropriate engagement tailored to its behavioral characteristics.</p>"
